   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The number of elements in the universal set, <span data-math=\"U\">U</span>, is <span data-math=\"n(U) = 48\">n(U) = 48</span>. Sets <span data-math=\"A\">A</span>, <span data-math=\"B\">B</span>, and <span data-math=\"C\">C</span> are subsets of <span data-math=\"U\">U</span>: <span data-math=\"n(A) = 23,\\,n(B) = 25\">n(A) = 23,\\,n(B) = 25</span>, and <span data-math=\"n(C) = 17\">n(C) = 17</span>. Also, <span data-math=\"n(A \\cap B) = 15,\\,n(B \\cap C) = 12,\\,n(C \\cap A) = 11\">n(A \\cap B) = 15,\\,n(B \\cap C) = 12,\\,n(C \\cap A) = 11</span>, and <span data-math=\"n(A \\cap B \\cap C) = 8\">n(A \\cap B \\cap C) = 8</span>.",
